 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -18,8 +18,34 @@\n     Every row must give the same number of features. The classifier is linear in the\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n-\n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    eps = 1e-10\n+    f = []\n+    # Squared features for all inputs\n+    f.append(x1 * x1)\n+    f.append(x2 * x2)\n+    f.append(x3 * x3)\n+    f.append(x4 * x4)\n+    f.append(x5 * x5)\n+    f.append(x6 * x6)\n+    # Log for lognormal x3 (guarded against non-positive)\n+    f.append(math.log(x3 + eps))\n+    # Sign features for pairwise products (quadrant detection)\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x1 * x2))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x1 * x6))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x2 * x6))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x3 * x4))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x3 * x5))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x1 * x4))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x1 * x5))\n+    # Threshold features for uniform [-2,2] variables\n+    f.append(max(0.0, x4))\n+    f.append(max(0.0, x5))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x4))\n+    f.append(math.copysign(1.0, x5))\n+    # Abs for sign patterns on uniform inputs\n+    f.append(abs(x4))\n+    f.append(abs(x5))\n+    return f\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
